                <pb facs="0563" n="478" sameAs="frus:frus1919v02/pg478"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">882.51/935: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of
                            State to the Chargé in Liberia</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Bundy</hi>)</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1919-05-20T18:00:00-04:00"><hi rendition="#italic">May 20, 1919, 6
                                p.m.</hi></date></dateline></opener>
                <p>Your May 12, 5 p.m.</p>
                <p>In view of loan negotiations and affairs affecting Liberia now under
                    consideration in Paris, suggest Liberian Government defer commissioning French
                    customs receiver until definite plans for the proposed rehabilitation of Liberia
                    are concluded.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Polk</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
